# Whether two intervals of the round-up interval are the same set (IEEE 1788 equal): the same lanes,
# or both empty; the default interval_rel_equal_1 on the meanings. Exact, in every rounding mode
# (docs/developer/design/upward.md, "Predicates and comparisons"). Requires the rounding mode upward
# set by kairn::upward::Scope and the options of docs/concepts/upward.md (GCC and Clang
# -frounding-math, MSVC /fp:strict).
kernel:        upward_rel_equal_1
rounding:      upward
input:         pair stored x = xu xn
input:         pair stored y = yu yn
output:        mask m
requires:      upward xu xn
requires:      upward yu yn
ensures:       certain m equal x y x=xu,xn y=yu,yn exact
min_precision: 1
source:        the lanes compared, and tests of emptiness (the listing of the round-up interval)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        unverified
domain:        extended
ieee_only:     yes
ieee_status:   unverified
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   the result is a mask, which has no non-finite value, and a comparison with NaN is false; certain states what comes out for every canonical operand

a = eq(xu, yu)
b = eq(xn, yn)
c = and(a, b)
ex = unord(xu, xu)
ey = unord(yu, yu)
ee = and(ex, ey)
m = or(c, ee)
